rows.en:
I was exhausted today.
I decided to go to sleep.
I crawled into bed.{p}

Just to test it, I closed my eyes, and the mask was floating in the darkness there, too.
But this was the mask in my memory.
It wasn't anywhere near as real as the hallucination I saw with my eyes open.{p}

No, I don't want that!
What am I going to do?
What should I do?{p}

I know, I'll read a book.
There was one I'd bought but still hadn't read.
I grabbed the book and flopped down on my bed.{p}

I caught my breath and peered into the book.
Now that he mentioned it, it did look a bit like him.
But how on earth...{p}

"It's {a}'s family."
"They look like {a}."
"Ooh, I wouldn't mind going with this one."{p}

"Stop! Keep your hands off my family☆"
As I screamed, I was pinned down.
"Who are you talking to? Get a grip!"{p}

This is no time for that★
If I don't do something about these guys, it won't just be me. My family will get hurt too.
"Let go! Let go of me☆"{p}

Somehow, I had a feeling she might want me to wear it.
I wasn't afraid.
I tried putting on the mask.{p}

The face of a man reflected in the glass...
This was the very face from the mask's memory.
I can't let him live.{p}

Maybe she wants me to burn it.
Maybe she has no more need for it.
I went out into the yard and set the mask down on the dirt.{p}

As I was about to go inside, I sensed someone.
What?
I turned around, but no one was there.{p}

This mask can't possibly be here.
I must still be dreaming.
I took a breath and focused my mind.{p}

"I've got something to take care of that day, so I can't make it.
Sorry, but I'm counting on you."
His words echoed hollowly.{p}
